// SeriesMetric Time-series metric (basic tier). blocks_behind = blocks behind, the larger of the highest block the node learned from peers minus its own height (same scrape) and the value the platform computes from this organization's chain head (scrape times differ per node, so values below the tolerance count as 0). txpool_added / txpool_removed / txpool_rejected = transactions per second entering the pool, leaving it (included in a block, replaced or dropped) and rejected. jvm_heap = percentage of Besu's Java heap in use (jvm_memory_used_bytes ÷ jvm_memory_max_bytes, area=heap). txpool_usage = percentage of the transaction pool in use (transactions in the pool ÷ the count limit; only the sequenced pool has a limit, so layered pools have no such series). txpool_oldest = seconds the oldest transaction in the pool has waited (0 for an empty pool; includes transactions stuck behind a nonce gap)
type SeriesMetric = MetricId

